  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "sfxnz's two-DGX-Spark vLLM TP2 recipe for NVIDIA's Qwen3.8 Flash Next NVFP4 checkpoint (snapshot fc694b54, the current NVIDIA revision) on the digest-pinned official vllm/vllm-openai nightly-aarch64 image (0.28.1rc1.dev437+ge962733e0). Upstream's two overlays are baked byte-identically: docker/ple_layer.py (qwen4_exp MIXED_PRECISION FP8 per-layer embeddings) and docker/modelopt.py (MTP FP8_BLOCK_SCALES and FP8_PB_WO load). In-band MTP-3 with the Triton draft MoE, BF16 (auto) KV cache, native 262144-token window, eight sequences (the only occupancy upstream measured), thinking off by default. Upstream measured 43.2 tok/s per stream prose and 55.5 structured at concurrency 1 on its own lab (claims, not measured here). Licences are information only: recipe scripts MIT (sfxnz), vLLM overlays Apache-2.0, model weights under the NVIDIA Open Model License. Vonk physical acceptance is pending.",
